# Pairs with EventualConvergence in ReplicationReBootstrap. A receiver restore re-stamps r's lineage;
# a sender that does not treat the new lineage as a gap never re-delivers what the
# restore removed (#4586).
MODULE: EventualConvergenceNoReseedOnReceiverRestamp
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a receiver restore requests no re-seed, so the receiver never regains what the restore removed
PERTURBS: RestoreR

--- FIND
    /\ restoredR' = TRUE
    /\ fellOff' = TRUE
    /\ booted' = FALSE
--- REPLACE
    /\ restoredR' = TRUE
\* MUTATION: no forced gap on the new receiver lineage.
    /\ fellOff' = fellOff
    /\ booted' = booted
--- END
